# Commit message casing

All git commit messages must be **lowercase**, including the type/prefix and subject.

```text
# ❌ BAD
feat: Update API Docs
Docs: Expand Introduction

# ✅ GOOD
feat: update api docs
docs: expand introduction
```

- Prefer conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `style:`
- Keep the full subject line lowercase (acronyms too: `api`, `sdk`, `mcp`)
- If the user supplies a message, lowercase it before committing unless they explicitly ask to preserve casing
